_[#11cce]","[#3cf0d]_#_[#92480]","[#92480]_#_[#11cce]"],"description":"These three neurons act together as Feed Forward Inhibition.  Our microphone neuron wil send constant signals to the two neurons below who will both star spiking. But after a few miliseconds, the inhibitory neuron will silence the bottom left neuron. This makes the bottom left neuron only fire once to trigger a behavior when SpikerBot first hears music!","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775578931222","neuronKeys":["[#11cce]","[#b85ab]"],"edgeStrings":["[#11cce]_#_[#0c435]","[#b85ab]_#_[#0c435]","[#0c435]_#_[#b85ab]"],"description":"When the delay neuron receives this single spike, it willwait, and send it to the other delay neuron. The spikes will ping-pong back and forth, making a simple dancing motion!","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775578985245","neuronKeys":["[#85472]"],"edgeStrings":["[#85472]_#_[#3cf0d]","[#85472]_#_[#b85ab]","[#b5f52]_#_[#85472]"],"description":"When it starts to get quiet and the music is over, SpikerBot will inhibit all dancing processes, and relax until the next tune takes over.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775579038253","neuronKeys":[],"edgeStrings":["[#b85ab]_#_[#057da]","[#0c435]_#_[#07e41]","[#0c435]_#_[#3535d]","[#b85ab]_#_[#3535d]","[#b85ab]_#_[#de24f]","[#0c435]_#_[#bc0f2]"],"description":"This dancer shimmies left and right, but what other dance moves can you come up with?","thumbnail":""}],"info":{"title":"Dance Partner","description":"SpikerBot will dance to loud music, and relaxes between songs.","author":"User","version":"1.0.1","timestamp":"2026-04-08T15:50:43.952956"}}